{"cluster_id": "C-2584", "topic": "A loose object at roots/<srid>/_files/x satisfies the current parseNamespaceFileKey", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B034-107"], "canonical_claim": "A loose object at `roots/<srid>/_files/x` satisfies the current `parseNamespaceFileKey` condition and is classified as a corrupt namespace file, causing `ca-decommission` to refuse and `ca-fsck` to report a hard `lifeless_keys` finding even though the key need not represent damage.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#loose-mountpoint-object-as-corrupt-namespace-file"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2585", "topic": "A custom CAS disk created through the inline disk(...)", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B035-042"], "canonical_claim": "A custom CAS disk created through the inline `disk(...)` AST function can remain cached in `Context` after its last table is dropped, leaving `ContentAddressedGC` and `MountLeaseKeeper` threads running against deleted backing storage; the lease thread can then raise a process-aborting `LOGICAL_ERROR`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L2207-L2267"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2586", "topic": "Without the heartbeat register, a slow-but-alive incumbent whose seq", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B036-013", "B036-014"], "canonical_claim": "Without the heartbeat register, a slow-but-alive incumbent whose `seq` changes only once per round can appear frozen across a follower window and be falsely deposed.; The B160 GC lease fix adds an advisory heartbeat register `hb`; a follower steals only when both `(owner, seq)` and `hb` remain frozen throughout its observation window.", "issue_ids": ["B160"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaGcLeaseCore_RESULTS.md#ca-gc-lease-core-results", "docs/superpowers/models/CaGcLeaseCore_RESULTS.md#sabotage-counterexample"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2587", "topic": "WipeEpoch alone can violate WriterEpochMonotoneUnique: after a write at", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B036-042"], "canonical_claim": "`WipeEpoch` alone can violate `WriterEpochMonotoneUnique`: after a write at epoch 1, wiping the durable epoch to 0 leaves `wrote` containing `(A,1)` while the live epoch is 0.", "issue_ids": ["rev.4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaCasMountCore_RESULTS.md#accepted-residual-gap"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2588", "topic": "The honest RemintEpoch branch's hardcoded epoch value 1 can", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B036-043"], "canonical_claim": "The honest `RemintEpoch` branch's hardcoded epoch value `1` can collide with a historical `(A,1)` already in `fencedEpochs`, allowing a live unfenced mount under a previously fenced pair and violating `FenceCostsEpoch`.", "issue_ids": ["rev.4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaCasMountCore_RESULTS.md#accepted-residual-gap"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2589", "topic": "The proposed slotOccupy composition cannot implement Occupied(bytes, token) because", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-020"], "canonical_claim": "The proposed slotOccupy composition cannot implement Occupied(bytes, token) because putIfAbsentControlled retries internally and resolveByExactGet throws CORRUPTED_DATA on a different occupant instead of returning its bytes and token", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r1_findings.md#L7-L9"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2590", "topic": "The v9 recovery and wedge paths must recheck the", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B028-050", "B036-046", "B037-123", "B040-027", "B041-021"], "canonical_claim": "The v9 recovery and wedge paths must recheck the captured mount-fence generation immediately before every mutation: `slot-occupy`, `_ckpt` publication, install, unwedge, or equivalent retry publication. The v9 mount recovery layer captures `(actor, generation, op)` identity at admission and rechecks generation after I/O before every publication; an `Occupied` `slot-occupy` result must be resolved by comparing bytes. The proven three same-value sites are slot-occupy, _ckpt CAS, and recovery install sharing one captured generation; the catalog token is a distinct ZombieGoLive credential Recovery must capture the mount fence generation at admission and require the same generation plus a non-superseded runtime for every slot-occupy, _ckpt CAS, and final install; remount must cancel or wait for recovery before rearming. Recovery installation and wedge retries are guarded by the fence generation captured at recovery start; a successor seal conclusively rejects an old-generation retry.", "issue_ids": ["r9-5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaCasMountCore_RESULTS.md#2026-07-28-recovery-generation", "docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-mount", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-tla-phase.md#L242-L258", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r1_findings.md#L19-L21", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r6_findings.md#L48-L54"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2591", "topic": "The actual three-site fence tests remain missing: Stage A", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-053"], "canonical_claim": "The actual three-site fence tests remain missing: Stage A recovery needs deterministic bumps after slot occupancy and before _ckpt, and after _ckpt and before install", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r2_findings.md#L19-L21"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2592", "topic": "Stage B Task 3 Step 1 still demands three", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-067", "B040-073"], "canonical_claim": "Stage B Task 3 Step 1 still demands three fence-bump-between-sites tests even though its credential framing requires separate generation-stale, token-stale, and both-stale catalog-site cases Stage B Task 3 Step 1 still includes only the generation-stale catalog-site case and omits token-stale and both-stale failing tests", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r3_findings.md#L7-L8", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r4_findings.md#L4-L4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2593", "topic": "A CAS request admitted before fence expiry can remain", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-210"], "canonical_claim": "A CAS request admitted before fence expiry can remain blocked through claim and grace and complete after recovery lists the namespace because attempt_timeout_ms is only a scheduling check, not a socket deadline", "issue_ids": ["O1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r3_findings.md#L1-L3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2594", "topic": "A fresh lease with min_active=0 and no prior R*", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-213"], "canonical_claim": "A fresh lease with min_active=0 and no prior R* does not safely cover prior-epoch builds; {0,0} is unsafe and a missing bound disables reclamation", "issue_ids": ["O2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r3_findings.md#L10-L12"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2595", "topic": "A required recovery floor stored only in an evictable", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-216"], "canonical_claim": "A required recovery floor stored only in an evictable ref-table runtime is lost under cache eviction or self-remount, and recovery can install after remount without a final supersession check", "issue_ids": ["N3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r3_findings.md#L19-L21"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2596", "topic": "The min_active and R* pair has no specified linearization", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B040-224"], "canonical_claim": "The min_active and R* pair has no specified linearization point because min_active and the ref allocator are sampled under separate synchronization, allowing grants after the sampled high-water to be swept", "issue_ids": ["O2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r4_findings.md#L10-L13"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2597", "topic": "The existing life_epoch allocator is server-root-wide rather than namespace-local", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B041-013"], "canonical_claim": "The existing life_epoch allocator is server-root-wide rather than namespace-local, so changing it for one warm rebirth would leave the mount lease on the old epoch while changing it for a full remount would affect every namespace.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r6_findings.md#L5-L20"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2598", "topic": "The ref layer still has read or removal entry", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B042-013"], "canonical_claim": "The ref layer still has read or removal entry points that recover and mint on demand: `CasRefLedger::dropNamespace`, `CasRefLedger::listRefs`, and `CasRefLedger::resolveRef` through `dropRefIfPresent`.", "issue_ids": ["D23"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/deferred-docs-fixes.md#d23-code-half-is-placed"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2599", "topic": "GcHeartbeat is the outlier in CAS format versioning because", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B043-072"], "canonical_claim": "`GcHeartbeat` is the outlier in CAS format versioning because it has no magic, version, or `CasHeader`; it must either remain explicitly disposable advisory state or adopt the common header convention.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/random_notes.md#lines-399-414"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2600", "topic": "A writer paused beyond its mount lease can pass", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-180", "AUDIT-M2-197", "B044-024", "B044-025", "B044-026"], "canonical_claim": "A writer paused beyond its mount lease can pass `mayMutate`, be paused before `casPut`, and then commit a shard mutation after another incarnation has claimed the mount because the shard CAS checks only a content token, not `writer_epoch`.; A VM clone or snapshot restore can duplicate `server_uuid` and create a dual-writer window until the original mount's next renewal detects the superseded `writer_epoch`.; Mount reclamation uses wall-clock lease expiry while the local write fence uses boot-clock time, so sufficient clock skew can let one server reclaim a lease that another still believes it holds.; SEC-7: the write/GC audit's fencing findings (J1/J2/J3) are attacker-amplifiable \u2014 an attacker who can skew a victim's clock via unauthenticated NTP can force a premature mount-lease reclaim and induce split-brain (J3), and an attacker who can induce a long stop-the-world pause (resource exhaustion, cgroup throttling) widens the unfenced `mayMutate()` to `casPut` window for a zombie write (J1); TLS protects S3 transit but NTP is typically unauthenticated. Recommendation: carry `writer_epoch` into the shard-CAS precondition, and require authenticated time (NTS/authenticated NTP) in deployment guidance.; CAS's single-shard `RootShard` register is linearizable only while single-writer holds, because the shard `casPut` is fenced by a content token, not a monotone `writer_epoch`; a paused/superseded writer (J1), a VM clone sharing `server_uuid` (J2), or wall-clock lease-expiry-vs-boot-clock skew (J3) each open a dual-writer window that produces split-brain / zombie-value / non-linearizable / forked-journal-history anomalies. This is the single headline register-level finding of the Jepsen/Elle-style consistency audit; the fix is to carry `writer_epoch` into the shard-CAS precondition, the same reject-if-stale pattern GC already uses on its `deleteExact`/`gc/state` CAS (which is why GC leadership is already split-brain-safe).", "issue_ids": ["J1", "J2", "J3", "SEC-7"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1016-L1028", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L425-L441", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L442-L446", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L447-L451", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L646-L646", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L768-L769", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L807-L828"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2601", "topic": "A process-local catalog_lifecycle_epoch cannot detect a catalog-life replacement made", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B049-027"], "canonical_claim": "A process-local `catalog_lifecycle_epoch` cannot detect a catalog-life replacement made by another `Pool` sharing the backend, so local epoch tracking is insufficient authority for cold runtime admission.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75c-runtime-cpp-report.md#important-fix-round-2-backend-authoritative-cold-runtime-admission"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2602", "topic": "Proposed fix for the Store::~Store() teardown abort: add a", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-031", "B013-005", "B013-006"], "canonical_claim": "Proposed fix for the Store::~Store() teardown abort: add a remount_shutting_down flag set under remount_thread_mutex at the very top of ~Store(); make scheduleRemount() check it first and refuse to spawn once set; re-join remount_thread after mount_keeper->stop(); and give MountLeaseKeeper its own destructor (stopBackground()) so the renewal thread is always joined before its std::function members are destroyed. `Store::~Store` must latch a shutdown flag before joining `remount_thread`, `scheduleRemount` must refuse to spawn after that flag is set, and teardown must re-join after `mount_keeper->stop()`. `MountLeaseKeeper` must join its renewal thread in `~MountLeaseKeeper()` before its `std::function` callbacks are destroyed.", "issue_ids": ["U#1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/review1.md#blockers", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L119-L139", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L82-L139", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L36-L43"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2603", "topic": "Before an F1 propagation fix, a read-only Store::open still", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-072", "B043-076"], "canonical_claim": "Before an F1 propagation fix, a read-only `Store::open` still called `PoolMeta::createOrValidate` unconditionally (`CasStore.cpp:122,134`), which does `casPut(..., expected=nullopt)` (create-if-missing, `CasPoolMeta.cpp:129`); over an EMPTY/wrong prefix this either mutates storage or throws a write-permission error instead of cleanly reporting \"pool absent\" \u2014 only the capability probe was skipped for `read_only`, not the meta write. Only bites read-only-over-empty; over a live pool with existing `_pool_meta` the call only validates.; `Store::open` should expose explicit create, read-write existing, and read-only existing modes so read-only opening cannot silently create `_pool_meta` or roots.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/refactoring-ideas.md#ideas", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-06-scenario-validation-night.md#notes"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2604", "topic": "An MSan log refuted the mount-fence observability spec's original", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-070", "AUDIT-M2-414", "B027-071"], "canonical_claim": "An MSan log refuted the mount-fence observability spec's original premise: the real failure mode was Mode 2, a hung lease-renewal call that produces a silently expired fence and a silent re-arm, with no throw and no log on any transition; the spec went to rev.2 to address this, and was specced but not yet implemented as of the writing.; The fence observability work covers both fence-loss modes: throwing renewal followed by self-remount (Mode 1) and silently hanging renewal followed by deadline expiry and late re-arm without remount (Mode 2).; For the mount-fence rev.2 silent-expiry path, Mode 2 coverage rests on the `setMountDeadline` signaler plus the Mode-2 ride-out test; the signaler is the load-bearing addition, since without it Part B never wakes on the dominant (silent-expiry) path.", "issue_ids": ["rev.2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-stage-b", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-fence-observability-and-write-grace.md#self-review", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-fence-observability-and-write-grace.md#task-overview", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-28-cas-fence-observability-and-write-grace-design.md#context-rca"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2605", "topic": "During rev.7/rev.8 disk-lifecycle implementation, T7's implementer review found a", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-115"], "canonical_claim": "During rev.7/rev.8 disk-lifecycle implementation, T7's implementer review found a real hole (I1): the observe/FSCK path could mint `_pool_meta` over a residual pool state, and the implementer's justification for why this was safe was factually wrong per the reviewer's independent re-verification; the fix flipped the polarity to fail-closed (mint-permission gate).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-22-unattended-rev7-lifecycle.md#t7-impl"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2606", "topic": "A transient CA lease loss could be misclassified by", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-162"], "canonical_claim": "A transient CA lease loss could be misclassified by the part-check thread as \"part looks broken\" and trigger destructive-shaped remediation; root-caused via correlated CA-log/part_log/text_log traces and fixed by pinning `TransientRefusalIsUpstreamRetryableTerminalIsNot` to call the real `isRetryableException` on both true and false branches, live-validated by reproducing the same blip against the fixed binary and observing zero \"looks broken\" lines.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/CURRENT.md#L2108-L2171"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2607", "topic": "rebuildBaseline (cas-gc-rebuild) has no mount-lease interlock: a live server's", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-177"], "canonical_claim": "`rebuildBaseline` (`cas-gc-rebuild`) has no mount-lease interlock: a live server's fresh mount lease does not stop rebuild from performing, because the tool's only live-server guard is the caller's own `isReadOnly()` flag, which cannot see a server mounted read-write on another host \u2014 contrasted with `LeaseConflictRefuses`, which does refuse on a GC-lease conflict. Confirmed as a real bug by the feature owner (\"Yep, this looks real... gc-rebuild i've added recently, and it almost untested\"). A regression test `CasGcRebuild.GCR1_NoMountLeaseInterlock_RunsUnderLiveMount` demonstrates rebuild running under a live mount; the fix flips the assertion to `EXPECT_FALSE(rep.performed)` with a mount-related refusal string.", "issue_ids": ["GCR-1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1190-L1229", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1276-L1276", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1479-L1481"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2608", "topic": "B160/P3-B1 required that a slow-but-alive incumbent GC leader must", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-325"], "canonical_claim": "B160/P3-B1 required that a slow-but-alive incumbent GC leader must not be stolen, and that the heartbeat must start at the exact lease-acquire instant to avoid a mid-switch soak wedge.", "issue_ids": ["B160", "P3-B1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#3-regression-pin-archaeology-bug-ids-invariant-encoded"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2609", "topic": "Writable Store::open validates server_root_id, claims the owner, allocates a", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B001-036"], "canonical_claim": "Writable Store::open validates server_root_id, claims the owner, allocates a durable writer epoch, validates the CAS request budget, claims the mount lease, starts MountLeaseKeeper, and arms the mount fence.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#L69-L84"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2610", "topic": "The owner object at gc/server-roots/<srid>/owner rejects a foreign UUID", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-079", "B001-052", "B004-048", "B021-021"], "canonical_claim": "The owner object at gc/server-roots/<srid>/owner rejects a foreign UUID and rejects re-claiming an absent owner over a non-empty data subtree with CORRUPTED_DATA. The server-root owner object is never deleted or reassigned; it binds `server_root_id` to one `server_uuid`, and an absent owner over a non-empty owned subtree fails with `CORRUPTED_DATA`.; `claimOwnerOrThrow` binds `server_root_id` to `server_uuid` permanently via a decision table: an owner present with a `retired_at_ms` tombstone throws `CORRUPTED_DATA` refusing to resume; an owner present with a different uuid throws `CORRUPTED_DATA` naming the regenerated-uuid-file cause and remedies; an absent owner over a non-provably-empty subtree throws `CORRUPTED_DATA` for identity-lost-over-existing-data; and losing the `putIfAbsent` race re-reads, proceeding only if the winning uuid matches. \"Provably empty\" requires both an authoritative catalog naming no life owned by the srid and 1-key LIST probes finding nothing under `cas/manifests/<srid>/` or `roots/<srid>/`.; When `claimOwnerOrThrow` finds an owner with the same `server_uuid` but a set `retired_at_ms`, it must throw `CORRUPTED_DATA` with a distinct operator message saying that the identity was explicitly decommissioned and requires deliberately clearing `retired_at_ms` for manual revival.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L45-L53", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#owner-claim", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-18-t5-owner-tombstone-design.md#L36-L39"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2611", "topic": "writer_epoch is allocated from gc/server-roots/<srid>/epoch by a durable CAS", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B001-053"], "canonical_claim": "writer_epoch is allocated from gc/server-roots/<srid>/epoch by a durable CAS bump and is strictly increasing across crashes and restarts.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L55-L62"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2612", "topic": "A live mount lease stores MountLease{server_uuid, writer_epoch, hostname, pid", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B001-054", "B004-049", "B004-143", "B005-005"], "canonical_claim": "A live mount lease stores MountLease{server_uuid, writer_epoch, hostname, pid, started_at_ms, seq, expires_at_ms, min_active, gc_fenced}. The object `gc/server-roots/<srid>/mount` carries both the liveness lease and build watermark, including `writer_epoch`, renewal `seq`, `expires_at_ms`, `min_active`, and `gc_fenced`.; The merged heartbeat body carries the existing mount fields plus `min_active_build_seq`, `observed_gc_round`, and `gc_fenced`; `observed_gc_round` is monotone and `gc_fenced` is terminal for the incarnation.; The merged heartbeat extends `MountLease` with `min_active`, `observed_gc_round`, and terminal `gc_fenced`; `UINT64_MAX` is the retired sentinel for `min_active`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L64-L80", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#mount-lease", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence.md#L416-L501", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence-redesign.md#merged-server-heartbeat-replaces-mount-object--watermark-object"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2613", "topic": "Before discovery, computeHeartbeatFloor fences out expired writer mounts so", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B002-011"], "canonical_claim": "Before discovery, `computeHeartbeatFloor` fences out expired writer mounts so their last commits are durable before the LIST sweep.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/04-gc-protocol.md#heartbeat-floor"]}

